Jove wrote:
>   Early GoP can easily save a character.  +6 damage per hit and +3
> to-hit.  Thrown rocks become deadly missiles at +8 per hit.  Bits of
> worthless glass do +8 damage per hit at one-tenth of the weight.  Expert
> +2 darts average +24 damage per fling.  +6 damage per hit can even make
> #twoweaponing reasonable.  Str:25 also increases the range of thrown
> weapons to 12.
>
>   That's better than an early +6 ring of increase damage.

It's not quite that simple.  Many characters will have +2 or +3 damage
from strength already; the +6 from GoP does _not_ stack with that,
while the +6 ring of increase damage does.

Put another way, if my str is 18/01 already, the GoP are only
equivalent to a +3 increase damage ring--they bring my damage bonus to
+6, while the +6 ring would bring my damage bonus to +9.

Regardless, early GoP really are great.  It's just that they're almost
never the best thing to wish for--though as I said earlier in the
thread I would consider wishing for them if I'd been lucky enough to
already have most of my essentials and more useful items like MR,
reflection, DSM, jumping boots, conflict, , etc and I was playing a
poor spellcaster with low str.  I'd probably still go with a magic
marker, but I'd at least consider them.

